1
00:00:11,782 --> 00:00:13,951
It's high time I chromed up.

2
00:00:14,035 --> 00:00:15,995
Get the fuck outta here.

3
00:00:16,078 --> 00:00:18,414
I already gave you the quote to sell.

4
00:00:18,497 --> 00:00:19,707
Not here to sell.

5
00:00:19,790 --> 00:00:21,625
I'm here to install.

6
00:00:21,709 --> 00:00:24,336
Listen. That's military grade.

7
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:27,840
You either got the build
to handle it or you don't.

8
00:00:27,923 --> 00:00:30,593
And choom, you don't got it.

9
00:00:30,676 --> 00:00:33,888
Spoken like a ripper
who cares about his clients.

10
00:00:33,971 --> 00:00:37,516
Hah! Snarky for a kid
who can't even afford me.

11
00:00:39,185 --> 00:00:40,811
Fuck you.

12
00:00:41,395 --> 00:00:42,730
Hold on.

13
00:00:42,813 --> 00:00:45,274
Fuck it, man. I'll bite.

14
00:00:45,941 --> 00:00:48,527
I'll chip you up.

15
00:00:48,611 --> 00:00:51,697
But when you come crying to yank it off…

16
00:00:52,865 --> 00:00:57,620
'cause it's poaching your brain,
I get the Sandy for free.

17
00:00:57,703 --> 00:01:00,081
So, ready to rip?

18
00:02:46,061 --> 00:02:52,234
At the convention, Lavabre attempted
to persuade Arasaka by using the…

19
00:02:52,318 --> 00:02:55,821
Martinez, David.
Your tardiness has been recorded.

20
00:02:55,905 --> 00:02:57,740
Get a load of this guy…

21
00:02:57,823 --> 00:02:59,742
Is he serio--

22
00:03:01,827 --> 00:03:03,913
We're at school you gonk!

23
00:03:03,996 --> 00:03:05,998
There are cameras. Have you lost your--

24
00:03:07,249 --> 00:03:09,043
Afraid of getting caught?

25
00:03:09,126 --> 00:03:11,128
'Cause I sure ain't.

26
00:03:11,211 --> 00:03:12,046
Come on.

27
00:03:13,005 --> 00:03:14,173
Well?

28
00:03:44,245 --> 00:03:46,330
Ow… That hurt…

29
00:03:46,413 --> 00:03:50,668
Ow… What did you do?!

30
00:03:50,751 --> 00:03:54,171
What kind of implant is that?
You broke my nose!

31
00:03:54,755 --> 00:03:56,423
You're done for!

32
00:03:56,507 --> 00:04:00,427
My father's an Arasaka exec!
On the Academy's board!

33
00:04:00,511 --> 00:04:04,598
Do you know how easy it'd be
to have you expelled?

34
00:04:04,682 --> 00:04:06,850
Like I give a shit.

35
00:04:31,542 --> 00:04:33,210
Is he serio--

36
00:04:36,422 --> 00:04:40,592
My father's an Arasaka exec!
On the Academy's board!

37
00:04:40,676 --> 00:04:43,053
Do you know how easy it'd be
to have you expelled?

38
00:04:43,637 --> 00:04:50,561
Marcus, why am I being shown footage
of my own son being assaulted?

39
00:04:50,644 --> 00:04:55,441
This student is David Martinez,
17 years old, from Santo Domingo.

40
00:04:55,524 --> 00:04:57,318
He is a top student at the Academy,

41
00:04:57,401 --> 00:05:01,030
but he was found using a bootleg wreath
that corrupted the Academy's hardware.

42
00:05:01,113 --> 00:05:04,491
He has no father and his mother was
recently killed in a traffic accident.

43
00:05:04,575 --> 00:05:06,493
He owes a considerable amount of debt--

44
00:05:06,577 --> 00:05:07,953
How is this relevant?

45
00:05:08,037 --> 00:05:10,205
Notice his movements…

46
00:05:10,289 --> 00:05:14,960
He has the Sandevistan that James Norris
had at the time of this death.

47
00:05:15,044 --> 00:05:18,255
The case that was filed
as a cyberpsychotic incident.

48
00:05:18,339 --> 00:05:19,173
Yes, sir.

49
00:05:19,256 --> 00:05:24,595
Yet, unlike the soldier, this student
displays no side effects from the implant.

50
00:05:24,678 --> 00:05:31,060
His tolerance for cybernetics could make
him a prime candidate to test the product.

51
00:05:31,769 --> 00:05:34,396
I see. And where is he now?

52
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,773
He was expelled, sir.

53
00:05:35,856 --> 00:05:36,940
Summon him.

54
00:05:37,024 --> 00:05:39,860
Lure him with the promise of
financial aid if you must.

55
00:05:39,943 --> 00:05:41,987
And what of your son?

56
00:05:42,071 --> 00:05:45,908
As my heir, it's high time he learned…

57
00:05:45,991 --> 00:05:48,994
what it means to serve
the company's best interests.

58
00:06:03,092 --> 00:06:06,386
I'm so fucked.

59
00:06:16,230 --> 00:06:18,899
Wash cycle complete…

60
00:07:46,236 --> 00:07:47,446
Come with me.

61
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:50,032
The hell is your problem?

62
00:07:50,115 --> 00:07:51,033
What?

63
00:07:51,116 --> 00:07:53,327
You're messing with my work.

64
00:07:53,410 --> 00:07:56,914
Work? Looked more like a picksocket to me.

65
00:07:56,997 --> 00:07:59,041
You some kinda badge?

66
00:07:59,124 --> 00:08:01,668
Can't believe you're a petty thief…

67
00:08:04,713 --> 00:08:06,131
Do I know you?

68
00:08:06,215 --> 00:08:07,966
No… not really. Just--

69
00:08:11,386 --> 00:08:14,556
Ooh, you're in trouble.

70
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:15,474
Huh?

71
00:08:15,557 --> 00:08:19,853
Really? A Sandevistan?
Not an off-the-rack model, either.

72
00:08:19,937 --> 00:08:23,690
I won't press you.
This is Night City after all…

73
00:08:23,774 --> 00:08:26,610
Crazy idea. How about we work together?

74
00:08:26,693 --> 00:08:27,903
What, stealing?

75
00:08:27,986 --> 00:08:30,864
I only steal from Arasaka suits.

76
00:08:30,948 --> 00:08:33,742
What about me then? I look corpo to you?

77
00:08:33,825 --> 00:08:37,246
My scan picked up an ID
from Arasaka Academy.

78
00:08:37,329 --> 00:08:41,416
But you're right,
you definitely don't look the type.

79
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,961
I dropped out.

80
00:08:44,044 --> 00:08:46,838
Oh? A bad boy.

81
00:08:47,548 --> 00:08:49,716
It's just 'Saka you target?

82
00:08:50,842 --> 00:08:52,219
You in?

83
00:08:52,302 --> 00:08:55,264
Gonna break poor momma's heart, y'know.

84
00:08:56,890 --> 00:08:59,017
Lesson number one.

85
00:08:59,101 --> 00:09:01,353
Less judgment, more awareness.

86
00:09:01,436 --> 00:09:03,522
Yeah, yeah. So, what's my cut?

87
00:09:03,605 --> 00:09:06,358
We'll split the haul 80-20.

88
00:09:06,441 --> 00:09:10,862
Fuck that. Don't you need my Sandevistan?

89
00:09:10,946 --> 00:09:13,365
But I'm the one pushing
the klepped shards.

90
00:09:13,448 --> 00:09:15,909
Plus, now I have a trainee to supervise.

91
00:09:15,993 --> 00:09:17,536
Trainee…?

92
00:09:17,619 --> 00:09:21,415
I'm actually tight on eddies right now.
Can't we do 60-40?

93
00:09:22,207 --> 00:09:26,753
70-30. And I'll pay you
the second the job's done.

94
00:09:28,297 --> 00:09:29,464
Fine.

95
00:09:29,548 --> 00:09:30,674
It's a deal.

96
00:09:31,508 --> 00:09:32,426
Call me Lucy.

97
00:09:34,094 --> 00:09:35,304
David.

98
00:10:47,834 --> 00:10:49,961
So? How did I do?

99
00:10:50,045 --> 00:10:52,839
I'd say you're well worth the 20%.

100
00:10:52,923 --> 00:10:54,341
It's 30!

101
00:10:54,424 --> 00:10:55,842
Kidding.

102
00:10:56,718 --> 00:10:58,345
Keep it rolling on another car?

103
00:10:58,428 --> 00:11:02,641
Maybe a different line.
By now, someone's probably noticed.

104
00:11:02,724 --> 00:11:04,601
We should keep the risk to a minimum…

105
00:11:07,604 --> 00:11:08,855
How bad?

106
00:11:08,939 --> 00:11:10,524
Rookie mistake.

107
00:11:10,607 --> 00:11:14,111
Hasn't taken any precautions
since installing that implant.

108
00:11:14,194 --> 00:11:16,071
Which immunosuppressant is he on?

109
00:11:16,863 --> 00:11:18,490
He insured?

110
00:11:18,573 --> 00:11:21,868
No clue. Doesn't look like he would be.

111
00:11:21,952 --> 00:11:25,664
Any family or guardian? Anyone I can call?

112
00:11:25,747 --> 00:11:28,875
Dunno. Parents, I guess.

113
00:11:28,959 --> 00:11:30,752
He used to go to the Academy.

114
00:11:30,836 --> 00:11:34,089
Arasaka? No wonder he could afford this.

115
00:11:34,172 --> 00:11:36,133
Hold on…

116
00:11:37,092 --> 00:11:40,011
Hey. How ya feeling?

117
00:11:40,637 --> 00:11:42,347
I'm gonna be sick…

118
00:11:42,431 --> 00:11:44,266
Which immunosuppressant do you take?

119
00:11:44,975 --> 00:11:46,268
Immuno… what?

120
00:11:48,353 --> 00:11:49,771
Wow, man…

121
00:11:49,855 --> 00:11:51,106
You're psycho.

122
00:11:55,277 --> 00:11:57,154
Hey, we passed the…

123
00:11:57,237 --> 00:11:58,447
Oh my.

124
00:11:58,530 --> 00:12:02,409
Listen, choom, the kid's got
an implant that'll fetch a nice price.

125
00:12:02,492 --> 00:12:04,035
Just sit back, relax and--

126
00:12:04,119 --> 00:12:07,289
What? You cut a deal
with the Scavengers or something?

127
00:12:07,372 --> 00:12:10,041
Sit back or I'll take your chrome, too.

128
00:12:10,125 --> 00:12:11,585
Sorry, David.

129
00:12:11,668 --> 00:12:14,796
Looks like your cut's down to 20.

130
00:12:29,352 --> 00:12:30,896
Let's go!

131
00:12:49,372 --> 00:12:50,290
Whoops.

132
00:12:50,373 --> 00:12:53,460
Hey, not dying, are ya?

133
00:12:53,543 --> 00:12:54,794
Doc…

134
00:12:54,878 --> 00:12:55,962
Huh?

135
00:12:56,046 --> 00:12:58,548
Doc's clinic… Please… take…

136
00:13:08,683 --> 00:13:10,060
David, buddy…

137
00:13:10,143 --> 00:13:13,063
You look like shit.

138
00:13:13,146 --> 00:13:14,231
Thanks…

139
00:13:15,482 --> 00:13:16,942
How many times you use it?

140
00:13:17,025 --> 00:13:19,319
Six… No, eight?

141
00:13:19,402 --> 00:13:21,363
Jesus Henry Christ!

142
00:13:21,446 --> 00:13:24,157
A grown-ass man
couldn't take that punishment.

143
00:13:24,241 --> 00:13:26,243
I was fine…

144
00:13:26,326 --> 00:13:28,453
But then my nose popped a cork.

145
00:13:29,037 --> 00:13:32,207
This gonk didn't know about
immunosuppressants.

146
00:13:33,083 --> 00:13:35,210
Didn't see the need.

147
00:13:35,293 --> 00:13:39,297
Of course you didn't.
Just sell him the meds.

148
00:13:39,381 --> 00:13:42,300
Shit off the shelf's not gonna cut it.
It'll cost ya.

149
00:13:42,384 --> 00:13:43,802
You good for it?

150
00:13:43,885 --> 00:13:45,554
You charging me?

151
00:13:45,637 --> 00:13:49,808
Fucking right I am!
Ain't running no charity.

152
00:13:50,767 --> 00:13:51,977
How much'll these buy?

153
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:54,938
Two days' worth.

154
00:13:56,231 --> 00:13:57,482
That's it?

155
00:13:57,566 --> 00:13:59,359
Plenty of other rippers out there.

156
00:13:59,442 --> 00:14:02,904
Of course, that might land you
back with the Scavs.

157
00:14:04,030 --> 00:14:05,991
Greedy bastard…

158
00:14:09,286 --> 00:14:11,997
You really don't want it gone?

159
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,206
Nope.

160
00:14:13,873 --> 00:14:18,712
Still can't believe it…
Eight times in one goddamn day.

161
00:14:18,795 --> 00:14:21,006
You're either a total masochist or…

162
00:14:21,089 --> 00:14:26,636
Listen. Don't use it more than
two times a day. Three max.

163
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:29,806
Even if your body can take it,
that egghead of yours can't.

164
00:14:29,890 --> 00:14:34,269
Your brain's gonna get scrambled.

165
00:14:35,395 --> 00:14:38,607
A single implant
could make me a cyberpsycho?

166
00:14:38,690 --> 00:14:42,193
Never heard anything like that before.

167
00:14:42,277 --> 00:14:43,528
Goes to show you…

168
00:14:43,612 --> 00:14:46,031
just how dangerous that thing is.

169
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,050
All done?

170
00:15:05,133 --> 00:15:06,343
Yeah.

171
00:15:06,426 --> 00:15:08,887
Guess that's a wrap for today.

172
00:15:08,970 --> 00:15:10,722
I can keep going.

173
00:15:10,805 --> 00:15:15,060
No way, I'm not babysitting a cyberpsycho.

174
00:15:15,644 --> 00:15:18,897
Only use the Sandevistan
when you really need to.

175
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:20,815
Lots of other ways to churn out eds.

176
00:15:21,733 --> 00:15:24,027
Still willing to work with me
after all that?

177
00:15:24,110 --> 00:15:26,947
Think I'd let you go
without being paid back first?

178
00:15:29,866 --> 00:15:32,577
Well, good. I need the eddies.

179
00:15:32,661 --> 00:15:33,870
That's the spirit.

180
00:15:35,538 --> 00:15:40,085
Sure you're not up for more tonight?
I'm kinda lagging on rent.

181
00:15:40,168 --> 00:15:42,879
No more today. Quit asking.

182
00:15:43,546 --> 00:15:44,923
Okay…

183
00:15:48,468 --> 00:15:49,469
Come with me.

184
00:15:49,552 --> 00:15:51,471
I knew you wanted to!

185
00:15:51,554 --> 00:15:53,306
Not work-related.

186
00:15:53,932 --> 00:15:54,891
Huh?

187
00:15:56,518 --> 00:15:57,519
Right here.

188
00:15:57,602 --> 00:16:00,230
You, uh… live alone?

189
00:16:00,313 --> 00:16:01,398
Yeah?

190
00:16:02,148 --> 00:16:02,983
Huh.

191
00:16:04,526 --> 00:16:06,194
Wait, are you nervous?

192
00:16:06,277 --> 00:16:07,112
No.

193
00:16:07,654 --> 00:16:08,780
Your first time?

194
00:16:08,863 --> 00:16:09,781
No.

195
00:16:11,282 --> 00:16:12,492
Hey, fuck off!

196
00:16:13,284 --> 00:16:14,244
Take a seat.

197
00:16:15,036 --> 00:16:16,913
I've only got beer. You drink?

198
00:16:16,997 --> 00:16:18,498
Uh, yeah.

199
00:16:18,581 --> 00:16:19,749
Cheers.

200
00:16:28,341 --> 00:16:31,886
Seriously? You've never drunk before?

201
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:34,014
No, I have. It's just…

202
00:16:34,889 --> 00:16:37,267
I don't like carbonated drinks or smokes.

203
00:16:37,892 --> 00:16:39,936
Do people like that really exist?

204
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:41,271
I'm not lying.

205
00:16:41,354 --> 00:16:44,190
Sure you aren't.
And what's up with that getup anyway?

206
00:16:47,819 --> 00:16:48,695
Take it off.

207
00:16:48,778 --> 00:16:50,238
What? Why?

208
00:16:50,321 --> 00:16:52,240
Just do it. Come on.

209
00:16:52,323 --> 00:16:53,158
H-Hey!

210
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,872
Don't mess with that…

211
00:17:01,082 --> 00:17:02,709
Edgerunners?

212
00:17:02,792 --> 00:17:05,170
It's another word for cyberpunk.

213
00:17:05,253 --> 00:17:07,047
It's who you wanna be, right?

214
00:17:08,298 --> 00:17:11,051
I'm actually a fan of JK's
"EDGERUNNERS" series.

215
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:13,303
You serious?

216
00:17:14,637 --> 00:17:15,805
Look who's talking.

217
00:17:15,889 --> 00:17:18,683
What's up with that tacky poster?

218
00:17:20,226 --> 00:17:21,186
You got a problem?

219
00:17:21,269 --> 00:17:25,065
Uh… no problem.

220
00:17:25,690 --> 00:17:29,944
Just always whacked me how those ads
make it seem like some kind of paradise.

221
00:17:30,028 --> 00:17:33,448
I mean, lots of peeps died trying to
turn that dumb rock into something useful.

222
00:17:34,032 --> 00:17:36,076
Sounds more like a prison than paradise.

223
00:17:37,202 --> 00:17:38,828
Sounds like someone did their homework.

224
00:17:40,038 --> 00:17:44,000
The Academy teaches you things
they don't show in the ads.

225
00:17:44,084 --> 00:17:47,045
As expected of a preppy Academy boy.

226
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:49,464
It's not like that.

227
00:17:49,547 --> 00:17:52,342
Isn't it? Never caught a pleb
attending a 'Saka school.

228
00:17:52,425 --> 00:17:53,551
It's not!

229
00:17:57,388 --> 00:18:00,475
My mom and I, we weren't well off.

230
00:18:00,558 --> 00:18:03,353
The Academy normally
wouldn't have taken me.

231
00:18:04,104 --> 00:18:08,733
But my mom had to work real
damn hard to keep me in.

232
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:14,114
You wanna know the kicker though?
I knew from day one that I'd never belong.

233
00:18:14,197 --> 00:18:17,575
Then why did you stick around for so long?

234
00:18:17,659 --> 00:18:22,580
Good fucking question. Guess it's 'cause
Mom wanted me to get a 'Saka job,

235
00:18:22,664 --> 00:18:24,499
climb the corporate ladder…

236
00:18:24,582 --> 00:18:29,587
That was her wish… Or dream, I guess.

237
00:18:29,671 --> 00:18:31,381
That's why.

238
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:34,843
That's not your dream, though.

239
00:18:34,926 --> 00:18:35,760
Not my dream?

240
00:18:36,344 --> 00:18:39,013
Well, yeah. You and your mom
are two different people.

241
00:18:39,931 --> 00:18:42,350
Why should you need to work for her dream?

242
00:18:43,184 --> 00:18:45,770
There's nothing wrong with that.

243
00:18:45,854 --> 00:18:48,148
You have to find your own dream.

244
00:18:48,690 --> 00:18:51,526
Sounds like you've found yours.

245
00:18:53,403 --> 00:18:54,529
You're joking.

246
00:18:54,612 --> 00:18:59,826
You called it a prison, but to me,
this city is a whole lot worse.

247
00:19:00,451 --> 00:19:01,619
Here?

248
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:04,789
I just wanna go away as far as possible.

249
00:19:08,042 --> 00:19:09,502
Lemme show you something.

250
00:19:24,934 --> 00:19:27,687
Whoa! Check the resolution on this!

251
00:19:27,770 --> 00:19:29,689
I can feel the fucking sun!

252
00:19:29,772 --> 00:19:33,693
It connects through your personal link
to let you feel the sun's heat.

253
00:19:33,776 --> 00:19:36,946
Of course, you'd burn to a crisp
if it was the real temperature,

254
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:40,450
so I made sure to tweak it down.

255
00:19:41,326 --> 00:19:42,327
Want me to change it back?

256
00:19:42,410 --> 00:19:44,329
No, this is fun!

257
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:46,831
You look ridiculous!

258
00:19:53,421 --> 00:19:54,547
Pretty cool, huh?

259
00:19:54,631 --> 00:19:56,257
This is amazing!

260
00:19:56,341 --> 00:19:57,383
Isn't it?

261
00:19:59,719 --> 00:20:00,845
Over here.

262
00:21:28,641 --> 00:21:31,352
First time I've ever shown anyone this.

263
00:21:31,436 --> 00:21:33,187
Oh… really?

264
00:21:34,731 --> 00:21:38,401
So, like… why me?

265
00:21:39,193 --> 00:21:43,448
No idea. Guess it just felt right.

266
